 schedules for cloud resources#Related#{2}":[300,300],"#Create Discovery schedules for cloud resources#Related#{3}":[301,301],"#Create Discovery schedules for cloud resources#Related#{4}":[302,303]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Discovery","target":"r-discovery","line":28},{"title":"Windows","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/mid-server-install-prereqs.md","line":64},{"title":"Linux","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/t_InstallAMIDServerOnLinux.md","line":64},{"title":"Use MID Server guided setup","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/use-mid-server-guidedsetup.md","line":64},{"title":"Cloud Discovery wizard","target":"cloud-discovery-wizard","line":70},{"title":"Discovery Quick Start","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/discovery-quick-start.md","line":84},{"title":"MID Server Guided Setup","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/use-mid-server-guidedsetup.md","line":86},{"title":"Migrate from CAPI to Patterns","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/migrate-from-capi-to-pattern.md","line":96},{"title":"AWS account ID","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/cloud-configuration-governance/aws-first-cld-and-srvc-accts.md","line":124},{"title":"Azure account ID","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/cloud-configuration-governance/azure-service-account-cloud-mgt.md","line":125},{"title":"GCP account ID","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/cloud-configuration-governance/gcp-first-cld-and-srvc-accts.md","line":126},{"title":"VMware account ID","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/cloud-configuration-governance/vmware-create-creds-cloud-mgt.md","line":127},{"title":"Alibaba Cloud account ID","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/set-up-alibaba-cloud-service-account.md","line":128},{"title":"Access setup for AWS service accounts","target":"access-aws-accounts","line":139},{"title":"Enable auto-refreshing of sub-accounts and datacenters","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/discovery-manager.md","line":179},{"title":"Discovery setup","target":"discovery-setup","line":186},{"title":"How does the \"Discover Virtual Machine\" \\(optional\\) work in Cloud Discovery","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0870860","line":211},{"title":"Discovery Admin Workspace Schedules","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/discovery-admin-workspace-schedules.md","line":260},{"title":"Discovery Home page","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/discovery-home-page.md","line":260},{"title":"Access setup for AWS service accounts","target":"access-aws-accounts","line":299},{"title":"Discovery","target":"r-discovery","line":300},{"title":"cloud discovery wizard","target":"cloud-discovery-wizard","line":301},{"title":"Discovery setup","target":"discovery-setup","line":302}],"metadata":{"title":"Create Discovery schedules for cloud resources","description":"Create schedules for discovering cloud resources using service accounts or IP ranges.Specify your cloud provider and select the service account to discover. You can include one or all available sub-accounts on a schedule. Provide the credentials for the cloud service account and test the connection. Cloud Discovery displays the list of available datacenters when you validate the service account. Specify which datacenters you want to discover through the schedule.You can discover virtual machines \\(VMs\\) during discovery of the cloud resources. Cloud Discovery performs a deep discovery of the virtual machines identified by the cloud schedule, using the IP addresses of the VMs.The final phase in the Discovery Manager wizard creates the schedule that triggers discovery of the cloud resources.Configure the Cloud Discovery to auto-refresh the list of sub-accounts and datacenters before each scheduled discovery. If Cloud Discovery identifies any new sub-accounts or datacenters, it adds them to the Configuration Management Database \\(CMDB\\) and includes them in the discovery schedule.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-operations-management/discovery/discovery-manager.html","release":"australia","product":"Discovery","classification":"discovery","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-27","reading_time_minutes":13,"breadcrumb":["Discovery for cloud environment","Discovery","ITOM Visibility","IT Operations Management"],"tags":["#it-operations-management","#discovery","#cmdb","#patterns","#ci","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/it-operations-management/discovery/discovery-manager.md"},
